#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:213
#: 0a2863cae1b34f69a591403d00f18459
msgid "Verification before testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:215
#: a2ee2ea532264c8495cf98c358c69d6d
msgid "To verify that ArduPilot is receiving ``VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE`` messages, on Mission Planner: press ``Ctrl+F`` and click on “Mavlink Inspector”, you should be able to see data coming in. The confidence level can be viewed in message ``VISION_POSITION_DELTA``, field ``confidence``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:220
#: 40ea1ee7cf634ed8aa9299c8cc2661de
msgid "Changes in value of the tracking confidence level can also be notified on Mission Planner’s message panel, HUD and by speech. These notifications will pop up when the system starts and when confidence level changes to a new state, for example from ``Medium`` to ``High``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:222
#: 2dff8fcd776a4bb2898e3ef99095af72
msgid "To enable speech in Mission Planner: Tab Config/Tuning > Planner > Speech > tick on \"Enable speech\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:223
#: acc44c99e9bc448387e1ebbcff141e7d
msgid "If there are some messages constantly displayed on the HUD, you might not be able to see / hear the confidence level notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:224
#: f73fc911f0d44d5297dea2ab16df6ac9
msgid "If telemetry is slow, notification might be dropped. You can still see the latest message in MAVLink Inspector, message ``STATUSTEXT``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:225
#: 44b487a753e447b2b5cc5feb015f531d
msgid "If telemetry is very slow, it may be flooded by VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE messages. You can disable message forwarding by setting bit 10 in ``SERIALx_OPTIONS``. Be aware you will not receive VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE in GCS anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:229
#: 832b92388bfd40a084de223b0b46f5ae
msgid "Ground Test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:231
#: cbb5f5e456c248f9be0c89de51b61bb6
msgid "After power on, ssh into the companion computer, navigate to the script and run: ``python3 t265_to_mavlink.py``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:233
#: b939c4ba36a748e2b6ba5828e9050891
msgid "Wait until the quadcopter icon appears on the map of Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:235
#: 0fc25dece2dc420b9a565b1e0fb5d321
msgid "Pick-up the vehicle and walk it around, check that the vehicle’s position movements are shown on the map. The trajectory of the vehicle on the map should reflect the real movements without too much distortion or overshoot. Below is an example of walking in a 2m x 2m square."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:240
#: 27dfab687d2745b3a28e5d82b55e4094
msgid "During the test, view the confidence level and verify tracking performance. For most applications you should trust the full 6dof pose only in **high** confidence. If you only need the rotation (3dof), lower confidence poses can be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:242
#: 1dc7e43aec724e4f84df36eecf8910f3
msgid "If the external navigation data is lost for any reason (tracking lost, script is interrupted etc.), reboot the Autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:246
#: fe24b0f28ef84e7a9cce5c290d68fc4a
msgid "If you are flying in a confined environment, it might be best to go around the safety perimeter of flying, view the trajectory on the map, then remember not to fly/setup mission beyond that perimeter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:249
#: df8ae06133644bd49f71fed8716c0845
msgid "Flight Test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:251
#: 107ea2e20223417fb13fac885da2ce6d
msgid "For your first flight:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:253
#: 52d088840b3a4c84b0cdd190685801b6
msgid "Takeoff in Stabilize or Alt-Hold, check that the vehicle is stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:255
#: a48a5e7217c3425a94a7d4485777e3e3
msgid "Move the vehicle around and observe the position on Mission Planner to see if tracking is stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:257
#: f96e8b8e803b4230b82da84c66ba13cc
msgid "Switch to Loiter, but always ready to switch back to Stabilize/Alt-Hold if anything goes awry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:259
#: 308d9d675b014386a92487abb6ec2bfb
msgid "Otherwise, the vehicle should hover stably and able to keep its position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:261
#: a08a301176304e83a4204d16a8ae7089
msgid "Move the vehicle around (translate, rotate) at varying speed, always ready to switch back to Stabilize/Alt-Hold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-vio-tracking-camera.rst:263
#: d8698e6e083d4f2f8cad10f74234d221
msgid "If everything works as expected, next time you can arm and takeoff in Loiter mode."
